From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Tracz <t@t90.dev>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/38] fix: disable generic VeriMark temperature cutoff

The VeriMark Desktop does not expose a temperature model to libfprint.
The generic three-minute cutoff therefore eventually disables the device
while the lock screen keeps identify available across a long session.
The driver already controls the device's active lifetime per operation, so
use libfprint's explicit opt-out for devices that can run continuously.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 396a7308..4432057d 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2824,4 +2824,5 @@ static void fpi_device_verimark_class_init(FpiDeviceVerimarkClass *klass)
     dev_class->list     = verimark_list;
     dev_class->delete   = verimark_delete;
     dev_class->cancel   = verimark_cancel;
+    dev_class->temp_hot_seconds = -1;
 }
